<title>CHINA: NEW ISLAND YEARLY NET PROFIT UP 13 PCT.</title>
<headline>NEW ISLAND YEARLY NET PROFIT UP 13 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   28.7   vs 25.5 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    5.0    vs 4.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    63.19  vs 56.02</p>
<p>    Turnover		     383.92 vs 330.60 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		 New Island Printing Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 15-19</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 3</p>
<p>NOTE - New Island is a packaging maker.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings have been adjusted for the one-for-10 bonus issue.</p>
<p>An amount of HK$3.80 million representing a refund of value added tax received from the People's Republic of China has been excluded from the 1996 turnover in line with the current year presentation.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nine H.K. cents (including interim dividend of four cents) vs eight cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
